and just about our size as it were,

00:57:35.420 --> 00:57:36.730
our scale that

00:57:38.350 --> 00:57:40.810
explains why you get
some kind of modularity

00:57:40.810 --> 00:57:42.710
and realization independence.

00:57:42.710 --> 00:57:45.460
It might be that the correct
story about those things

00:57:45.460 --> 00:57:48.380
for non-biological systems has
to be a little bit different.

00:57:48.380 --> 00:57:49.213
I don't know.

00:57:50.187 --> 00:57:51.490
- Can I add something to that though?

00:57:51.490 --> 00:57:54.700
Because it nests right
with what you were saying.

00:57:54.700 --> 00:57:55.620
If you ask,

00:57:55.620 --> 00:57:59.550
and this is something that I
wondered about for a while too,

00:57:59.550 --> 00:58:00.540
if you ask,

00:58:00.540 --> 00:58:03.370
is there some increase in fitness

00:58:03.370 --> 00:58:07.170
that one would get by being
able to see right down

00:58:07.170 --> 00:58:09.540
to the microscopic fabric of the world,

00:58:09.540 --> 00:58:11.810
and in particular epistemic fitness,

00:58:11.810 --> 00:58:16.360
would it add to my ability
to predict microscopically

00:58:16.360 --> 00:58:20.610
if I had microscopic rather
than merely macroscopic access

00:58:20.610 --> 00:58:22.370
to the systems in my environment?

00:58:22.370 --> 00:58:24.750
It turns out, for reasons
that are directly connected

00:58:24.750 --> 00:58:27.823
to the past hypothesis,
that the answer is no.

00:58:29.866 --> 00:58:32.990
And the answer is no precisely because

00:58:32.990 --> 00:58:34.740
of the microscopic, okay?

00:58:34.740 --> 00:58:37.090
So one of the interesting and important

00:58:37.090 --> 00:58:38.930
and profound things,

00:58:38.930 --> 00:58:42.560
and surprising things about thermodynamics

00:58:42.560 --> 00:58:43.770
is the one that you pointed to.

00:58:43.770 --> 00:58:46.420
There's no reason to think
from first principles

00:58:46.420 --> 00:58:49.170
that there should be
any kind of prediction

00:58:49.170 --> 00:58:53.150
at the macro level that wasn't
sensitive to microscopic.

00:58:53.150 --> 00:58:53.983
The fact

00:58:55.109 --> 00:58:57.190
that there are laws of thermodynamics,

00:58:57.190 --> 00:59:01.130
so as we can formulate
macroscopic generalizations

00:59:01.130 --> 00:59:04.240
that are insensitive to the
microscopic underpinnings

00:59:04.240 --> 00:59:07.120
is surprising, but it also means,

00:59:07.120 --> 00:59:11.220
because it means that
they're robust in the face of

00:59:11.220 --> 00:59:12.930
whatever's going on microscopically.

00:59:12.930 --> 00:59:15.600
But it also means that those
are the very generalizations

00:59:15.600 --> 00:59:17.993
that we rely on to predict the future.

00:59:19.930 --> 00:59:24.110
So having more information
about the microscopic state

00:59:24.110 --> 00:59:26.860
is not gonna be parlayable, so to speak,

00:59:26.860 --> 00:59:30.513
into increased macroscopic
prediction about the future.

00:59:33.670 --> 00:59:36.110
- Right, and so you're arguing that

00:59:36.110 --> 00:59:38.320
this is why sort of the modularity,

00:59:38.320 --> 00:59:40.300
this is where the modularity comes in,

00:59:40.300 --> 00:59:44.510
that you don't really
need to have descriptions

00:59:44.510 --> 00:59:46.053
for every possible,

00:59:47.030 --> 00:59:49.330
at the microscopic level for any sort

00:59:49.330 --> 00:59:51.223
of macro phenomenon, right?

00:59:53.320 --> 00:59:55.700
- Yeah, I mean, that's clearly true.

00:59:55.700 --> 01:00:00.300
And I get the kind of
reasoning you were describing,

01:00:00.300 --> 01:00:03.380
Jenann, has a role to play in that,

01:00:03.380 --> 01:00:07.773
but I guess I'm wondering
if that's the whole story?

01:00:08.665 --> 01:00:10.233
- Oh, most certainly
not. No, I think, yeah.

01:00:10.233 --> 01:00:13.970
- Does it have something
to do with the character of

01:00:15.433 --> 01:00:16.890
the generalizations themselves

01:00:16.890 --> 01:00:19.800
at the different levels, okay?

01:00:19.800 --> 01:00:21.730
So, you know-
- I'm sure.

01:00:21.730 --> 01:00:25.500
No, no, no, I think you're
thinking that everybody

01:00:25.500 --> 01:00:28.980
who's in the discussion
about thermodynamics said

01:00:28.980 --> 01:00:30.930
it's far more developed than it is.

01:00:30.930 --> 01:00:32.060
I mean, it's really,

01:00:32.060 --> 01:00:34.620
everybody knows that
there's so many things

01:00:34.620 --> 01:00:36.950
that we're only just
beginning to get a bit

01:00:36.950 --> 01:00:38.693
of a qualitative grip on.

01:00:39.600 --> 01:00:40.433
But you're right.

01:00:40.433 --> 01:00:44.610
I mean, even understanding
the target general,

01:00:44.610 --> 01:00:48.150
the target explananda much
less the precise nature

01:00:48.150 --> 01:00:50.420
of the thing that's gonna
be doing the explanation,

01:00:50.420 --> 01:00:51.870
and whether or not it's something

01:00:51.870 --> 01:00:54.990
that we can subsume under
the past hypothesis,

01:00:54.990 --> 01:00:56.087
are completely open questions.

01:00:56.087 --> 01:00:59.763
And I think almost everybody
would acknowledge that.

01:01:03.150 --> 01:01:08.150
- So if this is sort of a
natural moment to ask a question,

01:01:10.560 --> 01:01:14.120
Ty, did you want to read
out Ferdosa's question?

01:01:14.120 --> 01:01:15.563
- I think too, sure.

01:01:17.590 --> 01:01:20.950
He's quoting from "Causation
with a Human Face," Jim.

01:01:20.950 --> 01:01:23.720
There's no well-defined
notion of an intervention

01:01:23.720 --> 01:01:27.450
on the spin state of one of
the separated particle pairs

01:01:27.450 --> 01:01:31.740
with respect to the other
in EPR type experiments.

01:01:31.740 --> 01:01:35.490
This would represent a
limitation on the application

01:01:35.490 --> 01:01:40.080
of an interventionist account
of causation, end quotation.

01:01:40.080 --> 01:01:41.617
So Ferdosa's asking,

01:01:41.617 --> 01:01:44.420
"Would either of you care
to address this dilemma

01:01:44.420 --> 01:01:45.900
if indeed it is one?"

01:01:45.900 --> 01:01:50.767
And he says he know we're not
discussing quantum mechanics.

01:01:52.340 --> 01:01:54.010
- Jim, did you, since that's from you.

01:01:54.010 --> 01:01:56.530
I'm happy to, but I think
probably you're the person.

01:01:56.530 --> 01:01:59.850
- Okay, so that, just to clarify,

01:01:59.850 --> 01:02:03.150
that was from a paper of mine also

01:02:03.150 --> 01:02:07.520
with the title "Causation
with a Human Face" written,

01:02:07.520 --> 01:02:10.740
I don't know what, 10 or
15 years ago. (chuckles)

01:02:10.740 --> 01:02:13.930
And I don't, in present,

01:02:13.930 --> 01:02:16.970
subscribe to all of the views
about causation in physics

01:02:16.970 --> 01:02:20.503
that I defended in that paper.

01:02:22.610 --> 01:02:25.710
The paper's different
from the forthcoming book,

01:02:25.710 --> 01:02:28.740
but I will try to say
a little bit about this

01:02:28.740 --> 01:02:30.370
and the question of whether this is

01:02:30.370 --> 01:02:32.510
in some sense of limitation on

01:02:33.480 --> 01:02:37.330
broadly interventionist
conception of causation,

01:02:37.330 --> 01:02:39.730
I don't think so.

01:02:39.730 --> 01:02:42.920
I mean, one of the things that is clear

01:02:42.920 --> 01:02:45.300
in EPR type setups

01:02:45.300 --> 01:02:47.560
is that you cannot,

01:02:47.560 --> 01:02:52.560
by intervening on one of the
correlated particle pairs,

01:02:53.710 --> 01:02:58.710
causally influence the behavior
of the other particle there.

01:02:59.390 --> 01:03:03.773
Okay, this is a kind of
no signaling resolved.

01:03:05.240 --> 01:03:09.827
And so you certainly don't want the,

01:03:11.490 --> 01:03:12.490
I would've thought,

01:03:12.490 --> 01:03:14.290
the outcome to be that there's,

01:03:14.290 --> 01:03:17.070
or the correct way to
think about the situation

01:03:17.070 --> 01:03:19.470
to be that there's some causal connection

01:03:19.470 --> 01:03:22.243
between the two separated particle pairs.

01:03:23.080 --> 01:03:26.983
That would violate locality,
special relativity,

01:03:28.100 --> 01:03:29.360
et cetera, et cetera.

01:03:29.360 --> 01:03:31.940
So if it's right that there's
no well-defined notion

01:03:31.940 --> 01:03:34.010
of an intervention that you can carry out

01:03:35.260 --> 01:03:36.280
on one of the pairs,

01:03:36.280 --> 01:03:39.220
then the interventionist account
yields the correct answer,

01:03:39.220 --> 01:03:41.203
that there's no causal connection there.

01:03:41.203 --> 01:03:42.760
So I would see that as a virtue

01:03:42.760 --> 01:03:46.170
of the interventionist
account, not a limitation.

01:03:46.170 --> 01:03:51.170
But I will defer to the experts
on quantum mechanics soon

01:03:51.760 --> 01:03:55.790
who will know more about
this subject than I.

01:03:57.510 --> 01:03:59.400
- 100% agreement.

01:03:59.400 --> 01:04:01.610
And it goes very much with the idea that

01:04:01.610 --> 01:04:04.630
the causal relationship
part of the surface fabric

01:04:04.630 --> 01:04:05.870
of the world.

01:04:05.870 --> 01:04:08.760
And there are things that emerge

01:04:08.760 --> 01:04:10.640
when you have the right sorts of relations

01:04:10.640 --> 01:04:12.773
between interventions and outcomes.

01:04:16.130 --> 01:04:18.377
- Yeah, I mean, it's certainly,

01:04:18.377 --> 01:04:20.527
at least the way I'm
thinking about things,

01:04:21.478 --> 01:04:22.360
and maybe Jenann too,

01:04:22.360 --> 01:04:24.350
that it's an implication of this whole way

01:04:24.350 --> 01:04:25.980
of thinking about causation,

01:04:25.980 --> 01:04:28.890
that there may very
well be physical systems

01:04:28.890 --> 01:04:32.580
for which the kind of
causal analysis that we're

01:04:34.250 --> 01:04:37.050
employ in other kinds of contexts

01:04:37.050 --> 01:04:38.250
is just inappropriate.

01:04:38.250 --> 01:04:41.400
Because the preconditions
for the application

01:04:41.400 --> 01:04:43.840
of that kind of reasoning
just aren't present

01:04:43.840 --> 01:04:45.423
in the systems in question.

01:04:51.170 --> 01:04:55.100
So another question I thought
we might discuss, Jenann,

01:04:55.100 --> 01:05:00.023
unless someone else wants
to jump in and discuss-

01:05:00.975 --> 01:05:04.120
- I don't see anything, Jim,
so go ahead and proceed, yeah.

01:05:04.120 --> 01:05:05.850
- So you and I are both,

01:05:05.850 --> 01:05:08.270
I think, self-identified pragmatist

01:05:08.270 --> 01:05:10.283
of one variety or another.

01:05:12.210 --> 01:05:13.810
Could you say something, Jenann,

01:05:13.810 --> 01:05:17.677
about what are the distinctive commitments

01:05:17.677 --> 01:05:20.427
of your version of pragmatism and

01:05:21.870 --> 01:05:24.620
how does it contrast with
other sorts of possibilities?

01:05:26.450 --> 01:05:29.350
- I'm not sure that I have
any definite take on what sort

01:05:29.350 --> 01:05:30.510
of pragmatist I am.

01:05:30.510 --> 01:05:33.200
I tend to think that
we're natural creatures

01:05:33.200 --> 01:05:34.433
in a natural world.

01:05:37.320 --> 01:05:41.704
Our minds were made to
allow us to cope, not copy,

01:05:41.704 --> 01:05:43.270
as Rorty famously said.

01:05:43.270 --> 01:05:45.430
And many of the notions that we use

01:05:45.430 --> 01:05:46.470
to represent the world,

01:05:46.470 --> 01:05:47.450
even the ones that are kind

01:05:47.450 --> 01:05:49.640
of psychologically most basic for us

01:05:50.660 --> 01:05:52.940
in terms of how we represent the world,

01:05:52.940 --> 01:05:55.990
are just part of a user
interface that was designed

01:05:55.990 --> 01:05:58.350
to optimize our chances of getting around

01:06:00.542 --> 01:06:02.790
into feeding and mating opportunities.

01:06:02.790 --> 01:06:05.120
So in that sense, I'm a pragmatist.

01:06:05.120 --> 01:06:06.470
That sort of pragmatism,

01:06:06.470 --> 01:06:09.400
I think, is just a
consequence of naturalism.

01:06:09.400 --> 01:06:11.143
And it's one I was driven to.

01:06:12.320 --> 01:06:14.070
It was never a first principle for me.

01:06:14.070 --> 01:06:16.550
It was more one that I was
driven to you just by trying

01:06:16.550 --> 01:06:19.240
to understand how to fit creatures

01:06:19.240 --> 01:06:22.140
into creatures like us into the world

01:06:22.140 --> 01:06:23.560
as it's described by physics,

01:06:23.560 --> 01:06:26.960
and to reconcile the
manifest image of the world

01:06:26.960 --> 01:06:29.663
with the image that
physics presents to us.

01:06:31.230 --> 01:06:34.210
So that's the way that I think of it.

01:06:34.210 --> 01:06:37.070
Also, I mean, something
else that you've brought up

01:06:38.032 --> 01:06:39.630
that I think is right, which is

01:06:41.990 --> 01:06:45.340
the need to bring the
subject back into description

01:06:45.340 --> 01:06:46.990
when we're trying to understand

01:06:47.970 --> 01:06:50.120
even the most basic notions that we use

01:06:50.120 --> 01:06:52.250
to describe the world.

01:06:52.250 --> 01:06:56.410
And, I mean, in physics, I
think this becomes clear.

01:06:56.410 --> 01:06:58.173
So I come at, from a very,

01:06:59.219 --> 01:07:02.140
I started out being a fundamentalist
about physics thinking

01:07:02.140 --> 01:07:04.250
the world is the way that
physics describes it,

01:07:04.250 --> 01:07:07.600
but there are all these
problems coming up in physics.

01:07:07.600 --> 01:07:09.640
Places where some feature of the world,

01:07:09.640 --> 01:07:12.410
some feature of our
experience of the world

01:07:12.410 --> 01:07:14.790
or the first-person
perspective of the world

01:07:14.790 --> 01:07:17.220
or the everyday common
sense view of the world,

01:07:17.220 --> 01:07:19.070
that's somehow not locatable,

01:07:19.070 --> 01:07:22.340
or findable in the view of the world

01:07:22.340 --> 01:07:24.023
as it's described by physics.

01:07:24.960 --> 01:07:28.190
And in all of those cases or
all of the ones that I've-

01:07:28.190 --> 01:07:29.330
- And also, Jenann, I mean,

01:07:29.330 --> 01:07:31.050
even this fundamental thing, right?

01:07:31.050 --> 01:07:33.230
With quantum physics, which is the sort of

01:07:33.230 --> 01:07:36.500
the alleged clean separation
between the subject

01:07:36.500 --> 01:07:39.033
and the object, the
observer and the observed,

01:07:39.970 --> 01:07:43.130
when that gets disrupted as well, right?

01:07:43.130 --> 01:07:45.780
- Right. 100%, yeah.

01:07:45.780 --> 01:07:46.780
So one finds that

01:07:46.780 --> 01:07:49.540
the attempt to give us
sort of God's eye view

01:07:49.540 --> 01:07:51.930
of the world fails in ways that demand

01:07:51.930 --> 01:07:53.793
that you bring the subject back in.

01:07:56.180 --> 01:07:58.750
- So I had a question

01:08:00.040 --> 01:08:01.840
for both of you.

01:08:01.840 --> 01:08:02.700
This question about,

01:08:02.700 --> 01:08:04.910
I've been thinking about the modularity

01:08:04.910 --> 01:08:06.270
that Jim mentioned, right?

01:08:06.270 --> 01:08:08.970
That you can restrict
yourself to a certain level,

01:08:08.970 --> 01:08:11.570
macroscopic level about,

01:08:11.570 --> 01:08:14.490
I think it was the Kandinov
quotation that you said.

01:08:14.490 --> 01:08:17.330
You don't need to know QCD to understand

01:08:17.330 --> 01:08:18.960
how the bulldozer works.

01:08:18.960 --> 01:08:23.290
But, I mean, is that reflecting something,

01:08:23.290 --> 01:08:25.993
is that reflecting that the laws of,

01:08:27.780 --> 01:08:30.220
is reductionism somewhere in there

01:08:31.630 --> 01:08:32.920
as a feature of the laws?

01:08:32.920 --> 01:08:34.993
I mean, is that what it's about?

01:08:40.304 --> 01:08:42.590
- Were you asking Jim or me?

01:08:42.590 --> 01:08:44.043
- Yeah, well,

01:08:45.750 --> 01:08:46.950
so, I mean,

01:08:46.950 --> 01:08:50.153
I'm not sure quite what you
mean by reductionism but,

01:08:52.629 --> 01:08:55.977
I mean, the way I think about
it is it isn't that I'm not,

01:08:57.750 --> 01:09:00.970
and I assume this is the
way that Kandinov et al

01:09:00.970 --> 01:09:02.320
would think about it too.

01:09:02.320 --> 01:09:06.200
It's not as though you have
sort of emergent new physics

01:09:06.200 --> 01:09:09.650
at the bulldozer level
or something like that.

01:09:09.650 --> 01:09:11.530
It's rather more that you just don't have

01:09:11.530 --> 01:09:15.400
to take into account
certain kinds of information

01:09:16.340 --> 01:09:21.340
to model the behavior of bulldozers.

01:09:22.140 --> 01:09:24.250
So it's a feature

01:09:25.431 --> 01:09:27.631
of the world and our
fear rising that we can

01:09:30.070 --> 01:09:32.530
drop certain kinds of
information, there's.-

01:09:32.530 --> 01:09:34.730
- So some epistemic sufficiency?

01:09:34.730 --> 01:09:39.210
It is sufficient to
just know Newton's laws

01:09:39.210 --> 01:09:41.320
to understand what the bulldozer is doing,

01:09:41.320 --> 01:09:44.187
and you don't need to know QCD or QED?

01:09:45.597 --> 01:09:48.140
- Right, right, and I think

01:09:48.140 --> 01:09:53.140
this is related to other
kinds of generic facts,

01:09:55.410 --> 01:09:59.600
or, I guess, really sort
of semi-mathematical facts

01:10:02.701 --> 01:10:03.534
that are pertinent here.

01:10:03.534 --> 01:10:07.010
And, I mean, so you,
you can very often have

01:10:07.010 --> 01:10:09.930
a situation with a
funneling kind of structure.

01:10:09.930 --> 01:10:12.633
At a very, very fine-grain level,

01:10:14.140 --> 01:10:18.040
some set of variables are
relatively highly correlated

01:10:18.040 --> 01:10:23.040
with one another, but if you
coarse-grain in the right way,

01:10:23.170 --> 01:10:24.793
coarse-grain the variables,

01:10:25.890 --> 01:10:29.290
you can produce outcomes where

01:10:31.760 --> 01:10:35.150
you have just a much
smaller number of variables

01:10:35.150 --> 01:10:38.650
to begin with and you have lots

01:10:38.650 --> 01:10:40.720
of other stuff just becomes independent

01:10:40.720 --> 01:10:43.093
as a consequence of the coarse grainy.

01:10:45.750 --> 01:10:47.040
So, I mean,

01:10:47.040 --> 01:10:50.140
one of the things that I
see to be characteristic

01:10:50.140 --> 01:10:54.840
of causal inference is we're
exploiting independencies

01:10:54.840 --> 01:10:55.920
that exist in the world,

01:10:55.920 --> 01:10:59.100
both statistical independencies

01:10:59.100 --> 01:11:04.100
other kinds of independencies
of a more causal character.

01:11:04.180 --> 01:11:08.170
And the notion of independence
is very much a notion

01:11:08.170 --> 01:11:11.920
that's tied to ideas
about level and scale.

01:11:11.920 --> 01:11:13.263
So something can be,

01:11:15.374 --> 01:11:19.393
and you're modeling at an
incredibly fine-grain level.

01:11:20.630 --> 01:11:22.738
It can look as though everything

01:11:22.738 --> 01:11:24.470
is dependent on everything else.

01:11:24.470 --> 01:11:26.863
As you move to a more
coarse-grained level,

01:11:33.830 --> 01:11:36.370
you get, as I say, a
smaller number of variables,

01:11:36.370 --> 01:11:40.030
and you get other stuff, in a way,

01:11:40.030 --> 01:11:41.780
kind of effectively irrelevant.

01:11:41.780 --> 01:11:43.790
And effective here, in the sense,

01:11:43.790 --> 01:11:45.460
in which a physicist, I take it,

01:11:45.460 --> 01:11:50.184
would use the notion of higher-

01:11:50.184 --> 01:11:51.890
- And so, I mean, that's where

01:11:51.890 --> 01:11:54.510
this idea of an effective theory, right?

01:11:54.510 --> 01:11:59.510
So that you can treat some
variables as extraneous,

01:11:59.720 --> 01:12:04.313
and then you can formulate,

01:12:05.693 --> 01:12:07.010
you understand the behavior

01:12:07.010 --> 01:12:09.980
with a paradigm number of
variables that are independent,

01:12:09.980 --> 01:12:11.010
as you said,

01:12:11.010 --> 01:12:12.300
and that they are sufficient

01:12:12.300 --> 01:12:14.930
to give you explanatory power,

01:12:14.930 --> 01:12:19.409
predictive power, and so on.

01:12:19.409 --> 01:12:20.760
- Yeah.

01:12:20.760 --> 01:12:22.340
- Yeah, I think that's what I meant

01:12:22.340 --> 01:12:24.197
when I was trying to say reduction,

01:12:24.197 --> 01:12:26.630
you reduce reductionism

01:12:26.630 --> 01:12:30.110
and sort of an implementation
there of, yeah.

01:12:30.110 --> 01:12:32.500
- Yeah, so that's the sort
of picture that I have.

01:12:32.500 --> 01:12:35.190
You're looking for what a statistician

01:12:35.190 --> 01:12:37.890
would call sufficient
statistics. (chuckles)

01:12:37.890 --> 01:12:42.710
Where you have something that
is much higher dimensional,

01:12:42.710 --> 01:12:45.790
and you're trying to reduce it
down to a smaller dimension,

01:12:45.790 --> 01:12:49.900
but the smaller dimension still retains

01:12:49.900 --> 01:12:52.680
the relevant information that you need

01:12:52.680 --> 01:12:55.750
for understanding the macro behavior

01:12:55.750 --> 01:12:59.263
that you happen to be interested in.

01:13:00.483 --> 01:13:05.483
So that's the general
general picture that I have.

01:13:05.880 --> 01:13:07.420
And I must say that, I mean,

01:13:07.420 --> 01:13:09.890
philosophers have, of course,

01:13:09.890 --> 01:13:14.080
all sorts of ideas about
theory reduction, and so forth.

01:13:14.080 --> 01:13:17.120
I don't really see that a lot
of what the philosophers have

01:13:17.120 --> 01:13:20.680
to see about theory reduction
relates all that closely

01:13:20.680 --> 01:13:22.150
to what I just described,

01:13:22.150 --> 01:13:23.820
which seems like it's more of

01:13:25.530 --> 01:13:29.800
the relevant thing in
understanding how theories

01:13:29.800 --> 01:13:32.830
at different levels or scales
are related to one another.

